{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Ascend Mount Avarim.</b> Why is this juxtaposed here? Since the Holy One, blessed be He, said ״you shall give to them,״ he said: perhaps the Omnipresent has commanded me to assign the inheritance — perhaps the decree has been lifted and I shall enter the land? The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: My decree stands in its place. Another interpretation — once Moses entered the territory of the sons of Gad and the sons of Reuben, he rejoiced and said: it seems my vow has been annulled. A parable: a king who decreed upon his son that he not enter the portal of his palace — he entered the gate and the king was behind him, the courtyard and he was behind him, the hall and he was behind him. When he came to enter the chamber, he said to him: My son, from here onward you are forbidden to enter. (Sifrei)"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:01.567064750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}